WEBVTT

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.270
Forky, look.
Bonnie's right over there.

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:15.550
(GASPS) Hurry!

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.230
-(CHUCKLES)
-(FORKY PANTING)

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:21.510
FORKY: Whoo!

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:38.230
Huh? Woody?

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.550
Bo?

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.830
Woody?

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.550
Aren't we going to Bonnie?

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.030
I know, I know. But my friend
might be in there.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.270
Friend?

00:01:05.430 --> 00:01:06.950
Oh, a friend, uh...

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.590
Well, a friend is...

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:10.150
Well, a friend is
like you and me.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.310
-Trash?
-Trash, like... Yes.

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:13.950
And I'm very worried
that she might be lost.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.270
But, Woody,
Bonnie's right there.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.470
Yeah, we'll have you back
before she wakes up. Come on.

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.670
(WOODY GRUNTING)

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:29.590
WOODY: Bo?

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:30.910
FORKY: Bo?

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:33.630
Bo?

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:34.710
Bo?

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.390
-WOODY: Bo?
-Bo?

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.230
WOODY: Bo?

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:41.390
FORKY: Bo.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.950
Bo, Bo, Bo...

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.310
(FORKY BLABBERING)

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:47.030
-WOODY: Bo?
-Bo?

00:01:47.150 --> 00:01:50.630
(FORKY CONTINUES BLABBERING)

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:52.190
Can we go back to Bonnie now?

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.430
I don't see your friend.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:55.070
Yeah, okay.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:56.550
She's not in here.

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.910
Come on, let's go.

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.670
(WHEELS SQUEAKING)

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.870
-(GASPS)
-(FORKY EXCLAIMS)

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:10.430
Is that Bo?

00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.590
(BOTH EXCLAIM)

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.470
Uh... (CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)
Hey, howdy.

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:18.710
Hey there.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:20.230
Uh, sorry to bother you,
but...

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:22.190
GABBY GABBY: Why,
you're not a bother at all.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:25.310
We were just out
for my early morning stroll.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:26.590
And look... (GIGGLES)

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.590
we met you!

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:29.990
My name is Gabby Gabby.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.510
And this is my
very good friend Benson.

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:34.710
Oh, uh, Woody.
Pleasure to meet you.

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:37.110
Well, it's nice to meet you,
Woody. And you are...?

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:38.830
This is Forky.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.110
I'm trash.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:41.990
(STAMMERS) Our kid made him.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.230
Kid? Toys around here
don't have kids.

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.430
Are you two lost?

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:47.510
Lost? (CHUCKLES) No, no.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:50.390
But we are looking
for a lost toy.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.070
She's a figurine. Used to be
on that lamp in the window?

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.270
Name's Bo Peep?

00:02:54.430 --> 00:02:55.470
Bo Peep?

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:57.750
-Oh, yes, I know Bo.
-You do?

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.150
Hop on in.
We'll take you to her.

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:00.910
Oh, you don't have to do that.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.310
Well, okay.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.430
(WOODY GROANS)

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:06.870
Benson, be careful
with our new friends.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.110
Wow, what service.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.030
(OLD JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.150
Uh... (CLEARS THROAT)
Thank you for your help.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.230
I haven't seen Bo in years.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.150
May I ask, when were you made?

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:22.670
Me? Uh...

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:24.550
I'm not sure. Late '50s?

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:25.710
(GASPS) Me, too!

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:27.790
Gee, I wonder if we were made
in the same factory.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.630
Wouldn't that be something?

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.710
I gotta say,
you are in great condition.

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.910
Well, I try to stay active.

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.790
And look at that,
you have a voice box like me.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:38.950
Benson, show him.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.510
Oh, that's really
not necessary.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:47.790
VOICE BOX: I'm Gabby Gabby

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.750
(DISTORTED)
and I love you.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:51.950
Wow, you need to fix that.

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:54.950
My record works just fine.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:56.830
It's the voice box
that's broken.

00:03:56.990 --> 00:03:57.990
Does yours still work?

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.070
Hey!

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.550
VOICE BOX:
There's a snake in my boot!

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.870
Listen to that!
Let's see it.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.190
I bet it's the same type.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:06.590
(STAMMERS) No, thanks,
mine's sewn inside.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.230
Is Bo around here?
Because we need...

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.950
(CLOCK CHIMING)

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:11.750
GABBY GABBY: Oh.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.190
The store is about to open.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.350
Don't worry, we'll take you
where no one will see us.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.270
Oh, no. We can't stay.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.550
(GIGGLES) Yes, you can.

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.510
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.470
(FORKY WHIMPERS)

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.230
We gotta go.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:34.510
You can't leave yet.
You have what I need.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:37.590
Right inside there.

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:39.990
MARGARET: Returned that lamp
the next day.

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.070
HARMONY'S MOM:
You're kidding me!

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:42.870
HARMONY: Mom, can we go
to the park now?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.070
Harmony!

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:46.310
(WOODY YELLS)

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.350
Stop him, please.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:49.790
(PANTING)

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:57.110
(STRAINING)

00:04:57.510 --> 00:04:58.510
(GRUNTS)

00:04:58.870 --> 00:04:59.870
What's going on?

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.190
(FORKY WHIMPERING)

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:03.190
Come on! Let's go!

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:05.030
He's coming, he's coming!
I see him!

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:07.110
Forky? We got to get out of...

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.510
Woody!

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.270
(GASPS)

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:18.030
VOICE BOX: I'd like
to join your posse, boys.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:20.350
But first, I'm gonna sing
a little song.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.070
Grandma, look what I found.

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:30.070
-Can I take it to the park?
-Sure.

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.910
Mom, she has enough toys
from the store.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:36.230
Oh, it's fine.
Nobody buys the toys anyway.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:38.110
(GIGGLES) Thanks, Grandma!

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:41.990
-VOICE BOX: Yee-haw!
-(GIGGLES)

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.710
Mom, can we go
to the carnival?

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:46.310
HARMONY'S MOM: We're going
to the park.

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:47.390
Maybe later, sweetie.

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:51.510
(BIRDS CHIRPING)

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:55.750
Any sign of Woody?

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.150
-I don't see him!
-Shh!

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.190
(BONNIE MOANING)

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.070
JESSIE: Maybe we should
have gone with the fork.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:02.230
The spoon is safer.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.550
Mmm.

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:05.150
(ALL GASP)

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:06.390
(YAWNS)

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.470
(GASPS) Forky?

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:09.990
Where's Forky?

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.390
(WHIMPERS) Mom! Dad!

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:13.710
-What's wrong, honey?
-BONNIE'S MOM: Are you okay?

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.710
I can't find Forky!
He's missing!

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.270
Oh, Bonnie,
it'll be all right.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.110
I'm sure he's here somewhere.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.510
You know,
if you don't find him,

00:06:20.590 --> 00:06:21.590
you can make a new one.

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.830
No! There's only one Forky!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:25.110
BONNIE'S DAD: Uh...

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:26.470
Let's go look outside.

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:27.950
Maybe he fell on the ground
somewhere.

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:29.750
Oh, poor Bonnie.

00:06:29.830 --> 00:06:31.030
BONNIE'S MOM: We're gonna
find him, okay?

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.470
BONNIE: We have to find him,
Mom. He needs me.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:34.670
Woody was right.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.910
We all should have been
safeguarding the utensil.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.230
Why isn't Woody back yet?

00:06:38.310 --> 00:06:39.430
(GASPS) Do you think
he's lost?

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.070
-Buzz, what do we do?
-What do we do, Buzz?

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:42.830
Buzz, what do we do?
What do we do, Buzz?

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:44.470
-What do we do, Buzz? Buzz!
-I, uh...

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.110
-Buzz.
-What would Woody do?

00:06:46.270 --> 00:06:47.790
HAMM: Eh, jump out
of a moving vehicle.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.590
What would Woody do?

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:51.870
VOICE BOX:
It's a secret mission

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.550
in uncharted space. Let's go!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:56.310
I think I have to go.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:57.510
-Where?
-Where you goin'? Why?

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:58.590
TRIXIE: Should we all go?

00:06:58.670 --> 00:06:59.670
-Are we going?
-HAMM: And then what?

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.150
VOICE BOX: No time to explain!
Attack!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.590
No time to explain!

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:03.950
HAMM: Oh, no!
JESSIE: Buzz!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.030
Okay, what is with everyone
jumping out the window?

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:09.190
(GRUNTS)

